# `EKLC6Core.ent_le_HcondSig_of_phi_generated` — Pisa 7.40 with a generating *family*

`ent_le_HcondSig_of_gen` is the one-sided generator inequality

`ent μ (aDiag t ·) ≤ HcondSig μ A (comap (aDiag t ·) A)`

under the two hypotheses (i) `A` is `aDiag t ·`-descending (`comap (aDiag t ·) A ≤ A`) and
(ii) `⨆_n comap ((aDiag (-t) ·)^[n]) A = borel X₃`, i.e. `A` together with its inverse-`aDiag`
orbit generates the whole Borel σ-algebra.

In the geometric applications (Pisa 7.37/7.38, `EKLC6Core.exists_gen_plaque_of_mp`,
`EKLC6Core.exists_desc_plaque_algebra`) the σ-algebra `A` is *not* presented by its own
generation hypothesis, but as the σ-algebra generated by the *forward* `aDiag t`-orbit of a
countable Borel family `S : ℕ → Set X₃`,

`A = ⨆_n comap ((aDiag t ·)^[n]) (generateFrom (range S))`,

while the generation hypothesis available for the *inverse* flow is the analogous one for the
same family `S`,

`⨆_n comap ((aDiag (-t) ·)^[n]) (generateFrom (range S)) = borel X₃`.

The present lemma performs the (elementary) reduction: from these two hypotheses on `S` one gets
the two hypotheses of `ent_le_HcondSig_of_gen`, namely

* `comap (aDiag t ·) A ≤ A` (descending), because `comap (aDiag t ·)` commutes with the
  supremum and `comap (aDiag t ·) (comap ((aDiag t ·)^[n]) m) = comap ((aDiag t ·)^[n+1]) m`;
* `⨆_n comap ((aDiag (-t) ·)^[n]) A = borel X₃`, because
  `generateFrom (range S) = comap id (generateFrom (range S)) ≤ A` (the `n = 0` term of the
  defining supremum of `A`) and `A ≤ borel X₃` — the latter is the first field of the plaque
  algebra `hplq` (together with the Borel measurability of `aDiag (-t) ·`), which is what gives
  the reverse inequality `⨆_n comap ((aDiag (-t) ·)^[n]) A ≤ borel X₃`.
-/

