### What the statement really is (session 7 analysis)

Write `T = aDiag t ·` and `A` as in the statement.  Two facts pin the target down.

* `A = σ(S) ∨ comap T A` **exactly** (this is `hAg` read one step at a time:
  `⨆_n comap (T^[n]) σ(S) = σ(S) ∨ ⨆_n comap (T^[n+1]) σ(S) = σ(S) ∨ comap T A`).  Hence
  `HcondSig μ A (comap T A) = H(σ(S) | comap T A)` (the sup defining `HcondSig` is attained on
  the `σ(S)`-side).
* `HcondSig μ A (comap T A) ≤ ent μ T` **unconditionally** (`EntSig.ent_ge_HcondSig`): for
  `Q` with `partSigma Q ≤ A`, `Hcond μ Q (comap T A) ≤ Hcond μ Q (⨆_n comap (T^[n+1]) (partSigma Q)) = hPart μ T Q ≤ ent μ T`).

So the target is **equivalent to the equality**
`H(σ(S) | ⋁_{n≥1} comap (T^[n]) σ(S)) = ent μ T`, i.e. to `ent μ T ≤ HcondSig μ A (comap T A)`.
It is the hard half of Pisa 7.40/7.43, i.e. (via the already proved
`EKLC6Core.HcondSig_eq_growth_plaque`, which identifies `HcondSig μ A (comap T A)` with
`ofReal (∫ growthFun (Uminus t) ν t)` for *every* `aDiag t`-descending plaque algebra `A`) it is
**exactly** the inequality `ent μ T ≤ ofReal (∫ growthFun (Uminus t) ν t)` of EKL Prop. 3.1 /
Pisa 7.6(ii)+7.43.  It is therefore a theorem, but not an entropy-theoretic triviality.

### Why the hypotheses as written are not enough for a cheap proof

`hAg` + `hgenS` alone (without `hplq`) admit counterexamples: on the two-sided Bernoulli shift
with `σ(S) = bor`, `A = bor`, `comap T A = bor`, one has `hAg`, `hgenS` and
`HcondSig = H(bor|bor) = 0 < log 2 = ent μ T`.  Such an `A` is excluded by `hplq` (the atoms of
`bor` are points, and `shape bor U x = Stab_U(x)` is not of the form `O ∩ U` with `O` open for
`U = Uminus t ≠ ⊥`), so no counterexample is known — but `hplq` is a *geometric* hypothesis and
nothing entropy-theoretic in it forces the "capture"/finite-entropy structure that the source
obtains geometrically (Pisa 7.43–7.54, in particular 7.50/7.52 where `H_μ(Q̃) < ∞` is proved).

**Instantiation lemmas** (both `sorry`-free, axioms only `propext`/`choice`/`Quot.sound`):
`ent_le_HcondSig_of_generating_finPart` — the target from `σ(S) ≤ partSigma P ≤ A` — and
`ent_le_HcondSig_of_pastSig` — the same for the fleet's presentation `A = pastSigCutD t M`
(`EKLC6Core.cutDefs`), which is the shape produced by `EKLC6Core.exists_desc_subordinate` and
consumed by `EKLC6Core.isPlaqueAlgebra_pastSig_of_good_set`.  So all that is needed on top of
the existing geometric output is a finite partition `P` with `M ≤ partSigma P ≤ pastSigCutD t M`.

