many** atoms (`P` = the atoms of `σ(S)`: then `partSigma P = σ(S) = orbitSigma t P`), and more
generally whenever `σ(S)` is generated by one countable partition: this — the *generating
partition* of Pisa 7.43 — is the genuine missing input, and it is what the geometry
